{
  "dom_id": "question-129771",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Write the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin series for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,⋯\\,.$",
  "worked_solution": "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $2x$ in the above expansion and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & =1-\\frac{{(2x)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(2x)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯ \\\\  & =1-\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{16{x}^{4}}{24}-⋯ \\\\  & =1-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{4}-⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
